How to correctly prioritize alerts, triage them and comment on them.

An alert is a notification generated by a security when a specific event or sequence of events occurs.
When triaging alerts, these are the steps to take:
1. Understand who is under threat, like the affected user, hostname, cloud, network, or website
2. Note the action described in the alert, like whether it was a suspicious login, malware, or phishing
3. Review surrounding events, looking for suspicious actions shortly after or before the alert
4. Use threat intelligence platforms or other available resources to verify your thoughts
Note: Before begining to work on any alert, you have to first assign it to yourslef,d move the alert to "In Progress". If you cannot handle the alert as a SOC L1 analyst, you can escalate the alert to a SOC L2 analyst.
